  "claim": "The Grammy award winner for song for the year put out a 1971 album by the Carpenters and won an Academy Award for Best Original Song for A Star is Born.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Let Me Be the One (The Carpenters song). Sentence: \"Let Me Be the One\" is a song written in 1971 by Roger Nichols and Paul Williams.\nPage: Paul Williams (songwriter). Sentence: He is perhaps best known for writing popular songs performed by a number of acts in the 1970s, including Three Dog Night's \"An Old Fashioned Love Song\" and \"Out in the Country\", Helen Reddy's \"You and Me Against the World\", David Bowie's \"Fill Your Heart\", and the Carpenters' \"We've Only Just Begun\" and \"Rainy Days and Mondays\", as well as for his contributions to films, such as writing the lyrics to the #1 chart-topping \"Evergreen\", the love theme from \"A Star Is Born\", starring Barbra Streisand, for which he won a Grammy for Song of the Year and an Academy Award for Best Original Song; and \"Rainbow Connection\" from \"The Muppet Movie\".",
