        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "506e9f3c-c0d7-575c-ba19-c42c6507bde5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul Williams, Roger Nichols, Barbra Streisand, David Bowie, Helen Reddy\n- Songs: \"Let Me Be the One,\" \"An Old Fashioned Love Song,\" \"Out in the Country,\" \"You and Me Against the World,\" \"Fill Your Heart,\" \"We've Only Just Begun,\" \"Rainy Days and Mondays,\" \"Evergreen,\" \"Rainbow Connection\"\n- Groups: The Carpenters, Three Dog Night\n- Films: \"A Star Is Born,\" \"The Muppet Movie\"\n- Awards: Grammy Award for Song of the Year, Academy Award for Best Original Song\n\nFacts:\n- Roger Nichols and Paul Williams wrote the song \"Let Me Be the One\" in 1971.\n- In the 1970s, Paul Williams became known for writing popular songs performed by acts including Three Dog Night, Helen Reddy, David Bowie, and the Carpenters.\n- Paul Williams wrote Three Dog Night's \"An Old Fashioned Love Song\" and \"Out in the Country.\"\n- Paul Williams wrote Helen Reddy's \"You and Me Against the World.\"\n- Paul Williams wrote David Bowie's \"Fill Your Heart.\"\n- Paul Williams wrote the Carpenters' \"We've Only Just Begun\" and \"Rainy Days and Mondays.\"\n- Paul Williams wrote the lyrics to the #1 chart-topping song \"Evergreen,\" the love theme from the film \"A Star Is Born,\" which starred Barbra Streisand.\n- Paul Williams won a Grammy Award for Song of the Year and an Academy Award for Best Original Song for \"Evergreen.\"\n- Paul Williams also contributed to film music by writing \"Rainbow Connection\" from \"The Muppet Movie.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1f78cecb-24a2-5f89-901b-d8808ad37f2f",
        "text": "Page: Let Me Be the One (The Carpenters song). Sentence: \"Let Me Be the One\" is a song written in 1971 by Roger Nichols and Paul Williams.\nPage: Paul Williams (songwriter). Sentence: He is perhaps best known for writing popular songs performed by a number of acts in the 1970s, including Three Dog Night's \"An Old Fashioned Love Song\" and \"Out in the Country\", Helen Reddy's \"You and Me Against the World\", David Bowie's \"Fill Your Heart\", and the Carpenters' \"We've Only Just Begun\" and \"Rainy Days and Mondays\", as well as for his contributions to films, such as writing the lyrics to the #1 chart-topping \"Evergreen\", the love theme from \"A Star Is Born\", starring Barbra Streisand, for which he won a Grammy for Song of the Year and an Academy Award for Best Original Song; and \"Rainbow Connection\" from \"The Muppet Movie\".",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
